# R-mnbt2304-nccl-u924 — the deployed production profile.
#
# PROVENANCE
#   Reference: github.com/bumblebeers/dsv4-flash-2x-spark-deployment @ d4f9c48 (2026-09-14),
#   docs/STACK029.md "Recommended serving profile" -> profiles/K-ours-opt.env.
#   Every serving value is the reference's, except the justified deltas below.
#
# DELTA (1 of 4) — vision mm-prefix-span fix
#   With the V2 model runner, compute_mm_prefix_ranges derives mm-prefix bidirectional ranges
#   from PlaceholderRange.extract_embeds_range() instead of the full sentinel block, so image
#   rows leak into causal attention and predicted y collapses to the image centre.
#     before: y-slope 0.287, y mean abs err 19.09% (146.6 px); y pinned at 50.0
#     after:  y-slope 0.981 (r 0.999), y mean abs err 0.79% (6.1 px)
#   BOTH HALVES ARE REQUIRED. The overlay reads the two flags via getattr(..., 0/False) and
#   silently takes the UNFIXED branch when they are absent from the checkpoint config.json,
#   which they are. So MMPREFIX_FIX=1 alone is a no-op without EXTRA_ARGS.
#
# DELTA (2 of 4) — NCCL pinned-buffer reclaim
#   Four NCCL transport knobs: allocate 1 MiB connection buffers on 8 channels with Simple+LL
#   instead of 9.19 MiB buffers on the default channel count with Simple+LL128+LL.
#   Measured: worker `VLLM::Worker_TP` VmPin 2,495,520 kB -> 68,232 kB on both ranks, i.e.
#   -2.31 GiB/node, byte-identical across two independently loading ranks. No throughput
#   regression; gate battery PASS. Plain integers, not byte suffixes, because the profile is
#   sourced by bash and re-split on whitespace by the launcher.
#
# DELTA (3 of 4) — GPU_UTIL 0.88 -> 0.924
#   Spends the reclaimed memory on KV cache. Pool 3,756,959 -> 4,682,729 tokens (+24.6%),
#   4.466x the full 1M context. Validated by a six-rung GPU_UTIL ladder (0.899 -> 0.924):
#   2,400 requests, 0 failures, 0 instability events, 0 gate failures, throughput flat.
#   0.929 also passed but was rejected for spending the last ~800 MB of headroom.
#
# DELTA (4 of 4) — MAX_BATCHED 2304 + LPT 2048 (per-step fairness reserve)
#   MNBT is 2304, so the effective per-step prefill chunk is min(MNBT, LPT) = 2048, leaving
#   256 tokens of budget each step for other requests to decode or prefill. This spreads
#   first-token latency when a long prefill is running. To reproduce the plain reference
#   behaviour, set MAX_BATCHED=2048 and leave LPT unset.
#
# NOT DELTAS — deliberately restored reference values, with what they replace:
#   GPU_UTIL=0.88   (was 0.85)  reference value; 0.85 was a margin added on top of the baseline
#   MAX_NUM_SEQS=16 (was 12)    reference value; the 64-row FlashInfer dispatch boundary is real
#   K=3             (was 6)     DSpark self-speculation, +9-21% at every concurrency
#
# EXTRA_ENV is pinned EXPLICITLY rather than left to the launcher: expandable_segments:True is
# PyTorch's and eugr's default and is what the reference ran. Pinning it here means an upstream
# default change cannot silently move it. False was adopted 2026-09-23 for +616,169 tokens of
# pool and is the more fragmentation-prone mode — it trades away the mechanism that mitigates
# the prefill memory high-water mark.
GPU_UTIL=0.924; MAX_NUM_SEQS=16; MAX_BATCHED=2304; CAPTURE_SIZES="[1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,40,44,48,52,56,60,64]"
K=3; DRAFT_METHOD=probabilistic; EFFORT=high; LIMIT_IMAGES=8
RETENTION=4096; FORCE_A16=1; OVERRIDE_GEN='{"temperature":1.0,"top_p":0.95}'; PARSER_FIX=1; OPROJ=overlay; EP=0
EXTRA_ENV="PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True NCCL_BUFFSIZE=1048576 NCCL_LL128_BUFFSIZE=262144 NCCL_PROTO=^LL128 NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=8"
MMPREFIX_FIX=1
EXTRA_ARGS="--hf-overrides '{\"mm_prefix_span_leading_pad_modulus\":4,\"mm_prefix_clamp_sliding_window\":true}'"
LPT=2048
